# --- Generated data -------------------------------------------------------
# data/synthetic/ holds the CSVs written by data/make_synthetic_data.py.
# They are build products, not sources: the generator is deterministic given
# its --seed, so `make data` reproduces byte-identical files anywhere.
# Keeping them out of git keeps the repository small.
#
# The global patterns below ignore every common tabular / array / serialised
# data format anywhere in the tree, which makes it structurally impossible to
# commit a real-world recording *by accident*: git refuses to stage an ignored
# path unless it is added with --force.  This repository ships no data files
# at all -- only the code that generates them.  The committed results/*.json
# documents and figures/*.png images are not data files and are not ignored.
data/synthetic/
*.csv
*.parquet
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.feather
*.pkl

# The local list of identifying tokens that scripts/check_public.sh scans for.
# It must never be committed: see scripts/forbidden.example.
scripts/forbidden.local

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Packaging / build artefacts
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Test / coverage / type-checker caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# Notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Editors and OS -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Fresh verification outputs (published results are immutable inputs).
.work/

# Local reproduction evidence (never the reference results)
.reproduction/
